    "requirement": "The height of numerals and letters printed on the Principal Display Panel (PDP) must comply with Table-I limits.",
    "description": "Calculates package PDP area (rectangular side H x W; cylindrical 40% of height x circumference; other shapes 40% of total surface) and enforces minimum height of numerals/letters (A < 50 cm2: 1.0mm; 50-100: 1.5mm; 100-500: 2.5mm; 500-2500: 4.0mm; >=2500: 6.0mm). 1.5x larger if blown, formed, or molded on glass or plastic. Minimum width must be at least 1/3 height. Corrected row 1 molded PDP height to 2.0 mm via G.S.R. 1373(E). Proviso w.e.f 23-10-2025: Medical devices follow MDR 2017 character metrics.",
